2026-08-31T06:32Z claude note scope extended by the R29 ratification of 2026-08-31 (spec/DECISIONS.md): the corpus gains a cross-lingual slice, separately gated. Its thresholds are this ticket's to pin, and DESIGN.md 2.8 is where they land -- the ratification deliberately pinned no number
2026-08-31T11:54Z claude note WIDENED BY THE STEP 2-3 RULINGS (spec/DECISIONS.md 2026-08-31). Three additions to the exit criteria, each serving a term of goal 1. R33 needs three probe shapes the corpus does not carry today: a rare exact string no embedder would place near its query, a paraphrase sharing no content word with its answer, and an agreement case where a document both signals rank mid must come back above one only a single signal favours. R34 needs the answer sets read absolutely rather than as a stability set: every pinned answer within the first ten results, no tolerance, which is the opposite reading of the same fixture R21 uses. And the corpus must carry the INTERSECTIONS, not only one axis at a time: scale and language are independent everywhere except through the embedder, so a monster in a non-Latin script and a scale run at the multilingual default are where terms that look orthogonal fail together. The perimeter ruling also lands here: the fixture stands for what Zotero shows, so a group-library slice belongs in it and a trash or feed slice does not
2026-08-31T12:00Z claude note inherits tracker 0400's precondition role on its dissolution, 2026-08-31: no fixture library, no assertion, so every clause-level assertion in 0026 and 0032 waits on this corpus. The statement is not new — this ticket's body already carried it — and it is recorded here so the dissolution loses no reason
2026-08-31T13:38Z claude note THE FIXTURE'S LANGUAGE SET IS RULED (spec/DECISIONS.md 2026-08-31) and it is not the old five. MUST tier: English, French, Vietnamese — these carry R29's cross-lingual lanes too, since R29 binds an EN or FR query against Vietnamese content. SHOULD tier, one language per script and morphology class rather than one per community: Arabic (right-to-left), Russian (Cyrillic), Chinese (no word boundaries, and the platform two-gram geometry), German (compounding), Hindi (abugida, combining marks and conjuncts), Spanish (Latin with diacritics, standing for Portuguese and Italian). Greek leaves the corpus; Hebrew never entered it. The real cost is here rather than in the embedder: every candidate already declares all nine codes, but each tier language needs freely licensed documents and pinned answers in this corpus, and a public-domain Devanagari and Arabic set is work nobody has done yet. A SHOULD language whose corpus cannot be assembled is set aside with a stated reason, which is what the tier means — record the reason here when it happens
2026-08-31T14:13Z claude note THE FIXTURE MUST PIN ITS PASSAGE-LENGTH DISTRIBUTION, not only its documents and queries (spec/DESIGN.md 2.8, ruled 2026-08-31). R32's build bound is now a rate in milliseconds per passage, and a rate measured on one length distribution does not transfer to another: a corpus of short notes and a corpus of dense pages give different milliseconds for the same machine and the same model. So the corpus records its own distribution — passage count and length quantiles — beside the pinned answer sets, and a re-pin that changes the distribution invalidates the rate measured against it, the same way a re-pin that changes the answer set invalidates the golden run
2026-08-31T18:54Z claude note THE FIXTURE CORPUS GAINS TWO GOAL 1 TERMS (spec/DECISIONS.md 2026-08-31, MVP frame). R24's PAGE CLAUSE -- a hit leads to the page it came from, an estimated page saying it is one -- and R29 -- a query in English or French finds Vietnamese content with nothing translated -- are now terms, addressed here. R24 binds by clause: the page locator needs no segmenter and is already partly delivered, while the entry heading and the dedup clause stay out with experiment X5, so what this corpus owes is documents with pinned, known page ranges and not entries. R29 owes the cross-lingual answer sets ticket 0266 measured candidates against: EN and FR queries over Vietnamese content, with the negative control, gated separately from R7's monolingual lanes so a regression names which promise it broke. Both decide at BOTH levels under the same ruling's inversion, so the corpus is the surrogate and the author's own library re-earns its fidelity
